  "interpretation": [
    "Recovery uses nominal reference time with bounded host PID position pre-emphasis; finite arrival still waits for the exact original endpoint and stationary measured feedback.",
    "Identical recorded-route synthetic response at 40 ms improved from 15.32 s to 10.08 s; the 20 ms PID case reached ready in 10.14 s. Neither result meets five seconds.",
    "All cases ran 20 s of continuous welding and then 10 s of paused fixed-target holding. No physical motor, gravity, backlash, torque saturation or USB timing was simulated.",
    "Mechanical Hz is estimated from synthetic encoder feedback, not copied from requested or planned frequency. Per-axis travel is included because frequency alone does not establish tracking.",
    "The response time constants are provisional estimates from the earlier operator journal. Separate mismatched-response tests cover 0.5x and 1.2x recovery/welding and preserve the 3-degree pause at 1.5x.",
    "Wall-clock compute measurements include concurrent offline tests and exclude physical serial/CAN timing; they are not real-time or hardware qualification."
  ],
